/-!
# Galois cohomology of a finite field

Let `k` be a finite field with `q` elements, `Ω` an algebraic closure of `k` and
`G = Gal(Ω/k)`. For every `N > 0`, the roots of `X ^ (q ^ N) - X` in `Ω` form the unique
subextension `k_N` of degree `N` of `Ω / k`, whose Galois group is cyclic of order `N`, generated by
the arithmetic Frobenius `φ : x ↦ x ^ q`. Recording the exponent `a mod N` with `σ = φ ^ a` on
`k_N` gives continuous characters `G → ℤ / N`; for `N = ℓ ^ m` they are compatible, and define a
continuous character `χ : G → ℤ_ℓ` with `χ φ = 1`. Its kernel has finite quotients of order
prime to `ℓ`: if `E / k` is finite of degree `ℓ ^ b n'` with `ℓ ∤ n'`, then `k_{ℓ ^ b} ⊆ E`, and the
image of `ker χ` in `Gal(E/k)` lies in `Gal(E/k_{ℓ ^ b})`, of order `n'`.

Hence `(G, χ, φ)` is an `ℓ`-adic procyclic quotient (`DiscreteModule.IsEllAdicQuotient`), and
`Hᵠ(G, M) = 0` for `q ≥ 2` and every `ℓ`-primary discrete `G`-module `M`, for every prime `ℓ`
(blueprint `sk-lem-base-field-cd`).

## Main statements

- `FiniteField.mem_iff_pow_card_pow_finrank_eq`: a finite subextension of degree `n` consists of
  the roots of `X ^ (q ^ n) - X`.
- `FiniteField.exists_continuousMonoidHom_zmod`: the characters `G → ℤ / N`.
- `FiniteField.exists_isEllAdicQuotient`: the `ℓ`-adic procyclic quotient of `G`.
- `FiniteField.subsingleton_H_galois`: the vanishing above degree one.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe w u

open Module Polynomial

namespace FiniteField

variable {k Ω : Type*} [Field k] [Fintype k] [Field Ω] [Algebra k Ω]

end FiniteField
